    "stem": "Neel studies this cryptarithm. Each letter stands for a digit, and different letters stand for different digits.\n\n$$\\begin{array}{c@{}c} & A & B \\\\ + & A & B \\\\ \\hline & C & A \\end{array}$$\n\nWhich claim correctly narrows a digit before trying every full substitution?",
    "item_type": "mcq",
    "options": {
      "A": "Letter $C$ must be twice letter $A$, with no carry anywhere.",
      "B": "Any digits for $A$, $B$, and $C$ work as long as each letter is a single digit.",
      "C": "From the units column, $A$ equals the units digit of $2B$ after the carry is placed, so each choice of $B$ leaves only one possible $A$.",
      "D": "The sum $CA$ must be smaller than one addend $AB$."
    },
